ted the four commands with a one-line example each, so most of what the CLI does wasn't written down anywhere. This rewrites it around the three places it's used:\n\n- developing a frontend module with `openmrs develop`\n- building a distribution with `openmrs assemble` and `openmrs build`\n- the `rspack` and `webpack` commands and shared configs that modules build with\n\nEach section covers the options, the config file formats, and the behaviour that's easy to miss. For example, `build --fresh` also deletes what `assemble` wrote, the build config wins over flags except for `importmap`, `routes` and `defaultLocale`, and the default `importmap` and `routes` URLs are relative to the current page. It also links to the reference application's setup for serving the compressed copies and for filling in per-deployment settings with `envsubst`.\n\nA couple of current limitations are called out directly: `assets` in the build config is ignored, and relative local paths in the build config aren't resolved against the working directory. Those notes can come out when the fixes land.\n\nThe `--help` epilog had drifted as well. It said `configPaths` and `configUrls` are comma-separated (they're JSON arrays), described `spa-assemble-config.json` as the file both commands read, and was missing `routes`, `defaultLocale`, `env` and `frontendModuleExcludes`. It now matches the code and links to the README.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n## Related Issue\n\n## Other\n\nI checked what the README says against the code, and ran the CLI for the behaviour that was easy to get wrong, like `--fresh`.\n\nOffline support (`--support-offline` and `supportOffline`) is left out, since #1894 removed it.","nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b67a171-359f-49a0-9b7e-6e4d0484e013","uuid":"63f6edad-f185-438b-8bc3-4c518d27c890","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:21:27.140Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","number":1905,"ki